; Horse — AnimalDefinition data entry (gdd.md -> Data Schemas / Content Architecture).
; Roster row: roster.md -> Already-Defined Roster | Ruled: decisions.md -> D-43.
; Asset: Quaternius "Ultimate Animated Animal Pack", CC0 1.0 Universal — see
;   project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_animated_animals.tres.
; Source: source-content/assets/Ultimate Animated Animals - July 2021/glTF/Horse.gltf
;
; SPECIES: domestic horse (Equus caballus).
;
; CAPACITY FIELDS (D-43): capacity_radius = 0 -> SENTINEL `CAPACITY_RADIUS_FOLLOWS_SCOUT`,
; meaning "equal to scout_radius" (8), not a radius of zero. tiles_per_individual = 5,
; max_individuals = 6. Horse and Donkey were ruled apart on real ecology despite
; art.md proposing identical axes: donkeys are the more arid/rough-terrain-tolerant of the
; two, so Horse keeps open_grass while Donkey trades it for rocks. Farm-tolerant.
;
; fact_text is docs/content/cleared-pool-fact-cards.md § Horse's proposed line, transcribed
; verbatim — all four checklist steps PASS there.
;   "stand up on its own in about an hour ... walk just a few hours after that" -> ADW
;   Equus caballus, "Foals are born precocial and well-developed, usually being able to
;   stand within an hour of birth and walk within four to five hours."
; https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Equus_caballus/
; kids.nationalgeographic.com was checked and rejected: its only live equine page is
; Przewalski's horse, a different species — see the source file's retrieval trace.
;
; news_reports intentionally empty — News Report pools for this pool are a separate, later
; purchase (not part of Content Pipeline step 4/5 for this dispatch).
